<tmc-service-inc>
<pub id="RM0550J">
<servcat id="06">
<name>Brake</name>
<section id="1002J_S000U" variety="S000U">
<name>Brake Control</name>
<ttl id="1002J_S000U_744TG_T0089" variety="T0089">
<name>ABS with EBD &amp; TRC &amp; VSC &amp; BA System</name>
<para id="RM000000NC100QX" category="C" type-id="3030Y" name-id="442OT-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>C1381/97</dtccode>
<dtcname>G Sensor Power Source Voltage Malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000000NC100QX_05" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00007RC00000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>This code is output when there is a malfunction in the power source system of the yaw rate sensor (with built-in G sensor).</ptxt>
<ptxt>This code may be stored due to a temporary drop in power source voltage.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.50in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.81in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.77in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Output Related Items</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C1381/97</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>At a vehicle speed of 3km/h or more with the IG1 terminal voltage at 9.5 to 17.4V, a G sensor power source malfunction signal is received for 10 seconds or more</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Poor contact pressure, terminal deformation or corrosion of yaw rate sensor connector (IG terminal)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Yaw rate sensor (with built-in G sensor) power source circuit</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<table pgwide="1">
<title>Code Display List</title>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>SAE DTC</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>ABS Light Display Code</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>VSC Light Display Code</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C1381</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>97</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>43</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000NC100QX_06" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00007RD00000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C146386J01" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000NC100QX_07" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___00007RE00000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>If the yaw rate sensor is replaced, perform "Yaw Rate &amp; G Sensor 0-point Memory Clear and 0-point Acquisition" for the VSC system. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000001A8300PX"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If the yaw rate sensor is replaced, perform "AT/CVT Learned Value Initialization" for the CVT system, and always perform both "G Sensor 0-point Learning" and "CVT Hydraulic Pressure Learning". (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM0000021F400AX"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000NC100QX_08" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM000000NC100QX_08_0006" proc-id="RM0550J___00007RF00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness and Connector (Yaw Rate Sensor Power Source)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check that the yaw rate sensor connector is not loose, disconnected, etc.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the yaw rate sensor connector.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check that the connector case and terminals are not deformed or corroded.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>No deformation or corrosion</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the voltage and resistance between the wire harness side connector of the yaw rate sensor and body ground.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C146388J04" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Voltage</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.96in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.01in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.16in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>4 (IG) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10 to 14V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.99in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.97in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.17in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>1 (GND) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000NC100QX_08_0007" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000000NC100QX_08_0009" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000NC100QX_08_0007" proc-id="RM0550J___00007RG00000">
<scantool type="1"/>
<testtitle>Recheck DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Clear the DTCs. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000060000PX"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Perform a road test and check the DTCs again. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM00000060000PX"/>)</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.72in"/>
<colspec colname="COLSPEC0" colwidth="1.41in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>OK</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Sensor power source malfunction code is output again</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000NC100QX_08_0008" fin="true">A</down>
<right ref="RM000000NC100QX_08_0010" fin="true">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000NC100QX_08_0008">
<testtitle>Perform Problem Reproduction Test<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000ABY03DX"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000NC100QX_08_0009">
<testtitle>Repair or Replace Wire Harness or Connector</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000NC100QX_08_0010">
<testtitle>Replace yaw rate sensor assembly<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000003054000X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
</subpara>
</para>
</ttl>
</section>
</servcat>
</pub>
